## Findings
1. advisory — brief:35 [severity: S2] `reload()` now calls `setModelsSettled(false)`, and `onConfirm` calls `reload()` after every successful write. So each Confirm sends Seats back to `loading`, shows the "Loading the seats…" notice above the populated roster and announces it in the live region until `/api/models` returns. That contradicts brief:72 ("Seats only reports its existing independent model read as part of capture readiness") and `StatusInput.loaded`'s "the first read has landed", and no seats/states row covers status after a successful Confirm. Replace brief:35 with: "`apps/web/src/screens/Seats.tsx`: expose ready only after the first officina and first models reads settle; `modelsSettled` latches like `loaded`, so a post-write reload never returns the screen to loading; retain the existing model-result fallback." [class: spec×fix-opens-new-surface] — check: none: a `seats.spec.ts` row that holds `/api/models` after a successful Confirm and asserts no `.seats .screen-notice` and no `.shell__status[data-state="loading"]`
2. advisory — brief:61 [severity: S3] The sidebar's Needs-you badge is a second reader of the inbox truth (`App.tsx`'s own `fetchInbox`, D-070 C), and neither gate names it. On Inbox the screen's effect fires its read before App's, so a capture can precede the badge. Replace brief:61's limit with: "limit: the shell sidebar's Needs-you count (App.tsx's separate `/api/inbox` read) is not gated and is reused unchanged; the fixed sample fixture, API readers, Playwright locator waiting and font machinery are reused unchanged, not guaranteed (D-076 E); internal states outside the initial view remain W-341's scope." [class: spec×promise-contract-not-declared] — check: none: a W-360-b2 row that holds App's `/api/inbox` read and asserts the gate stays unresolved until `.sidebar__badge` renders
3. advisory — brief:55 [severity: S4] "Three equal metadata columns" is false: the CSS is `minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 0.8fr)`. Replace "roster rows use three equal metadata columns" with "roster rows use three metadata columns (`minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 0.8fr)`)". [class: spec×prose-contradiction-under-revision] — check: apps/web/test/w360.test.ts
